 "intro": "Near Noreia, in the eastern Alps (modern Austria), 112 BC. A vast migrating people, the Cimbri and Teutones, has entered the land of Rome’s allies the Taurisci. You are the consul Gnaeus Papirius Carbo. The sources are brief.",
 "debrief": "In Appian’s and Strabo’s accounts, Carbo ordered the Cimbri to leave and gave them guides, but secretly planned to ambush them on the march. The Cimbri learned of it and attacked his army near Noreia, defeating it badly; a thunderstorm let some Romans escape. The Cimbri did not invade Italy but turned west into Gaul, beginning a war that led to Arausio. Carbo was later prosecuted and killed himself. The other choices are what-ifs.",
